%I A399823 #46 Nov 07 2026 23:06:03
%S A399823 3,3,3,3,3,3,3,71,13,13,41,5,5,41,11,17,5,7,5,13,59,151,7,17,199,17,7,
%T A399823 3,103,59,311,103,107,3,7,61,13,3,5,433,3,5,29,227,269,13,59,7,179,3,
%U A399823 3,11,13,349,29,101,13,61,31,11,521,19,101,71,229,571,11
%N A399823 For n>=1, a(n) is the least twin prime that starts a block of 2*n - 1 consecutive terms of A077800 having a twin-prime sum.
%H A399823 Robert Israel, <a href="/A399823/b399823.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A399823 3 is the first twin prime in the chain [3, 5, 5], which is the earliest chain of 2 * 2 - 1 = 3 consecutive twin primes whose sum, 13, is a twin prime. Hence a(2) = 3.
%e A399823 71 is the first twin prime in the chain [71, 73, 101, 103, 107, 109, 137, 139, 149, 151, 179, 181, 191, 193, 197], which is the earliest chain of 2 * 8 - 1 = 15 consecutive twin primes whose sum, 2081, is a twin prime. Hence a(8) = 71.
%p A399823 LTP:= select(t -> isprime(t) and isprime(t+2), [3,seq(i,i=5 .. 10000,6)]):
%p A399823 TP:= [seq(op([t,t+2]), t = LTP)]:
%p A399823 PS:= [0,op(ListTools:-PartialSums(TP))]: m:= nops(PS):
%p A399823 f:= proc(n) local i,v; for i from 2 to m-(2*n-1) do v:= PS[i+2*n-2]-PS[i-1]; if isprime(v) and (isprime(v+2) or isprime(v-2)) then return TP[i-1] fi od; FAIL end proc:
%p A399823 map(f, [$1..100]); # _Robert Israel_, Nov 03 2026
%Y A399823 Cf. A001097, A013918, A053845, A070934, A071151, A077800, A400578, A400738.
%K A399823 nonn,new
%O A399823 1,1
